            <div xml:id="d247">

                <pb facs="0328" n="235" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg235"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.18/34: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-28T16:00:00-06:00">February 28, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation in Costa Rica: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“February 28, 4 p.m. Your telegram February 28, 10 a.m. I have advised
                            the Minister for Foreign Affairs that there will be some <pb facs="0329"
                                n="236" xml:id="pg236"/> delay in this matter but the attitude here
                            is such that I have thought it advisable to give him no further
                            information from your telegram or to make further representations in
                            this connection until I have received instructions from the Department
                            in reply to telegram I am sending it today. Repeated to the
                            Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
